WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.170
In high -performance and AI -optimized data centers, thermal management

2
00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.430
is no longer just a matter of airflow.

3
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.290
It's a fundamental design priority.

4
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:19.330
The ORv3 specification integrates both air and liquid cooling support

5
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.550
directly into the rack infrastructure, enabling flexibility across

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.690
deployment types and workloads.

7
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.970
Let's start with air cooling.

8
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:34.490
ORv3 racks maintain compatibility with traditional air -cooled systems

9
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:38.670
by supporting consistent front -to -rear airflow through the rack

10
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:44.270
and chassis. This ensures that even legacy or mixed environment

11
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:49.310
deployments remain viable, allowing a gradual transition to advanced

12
00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:52.170
cooling without a full infrastructure overhaul.

13
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:58.570
However, as compute densities rise, especially in AI, HPC,

14
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:03.490
and GPU -intensive environments, air alone isn't sufficient.

15
00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.790
That's where liquid cooling enters the frame.

16
00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.990
ORv3 introduces native support for Direct Liquid Cooling, or DLC,

17
00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.470
through a robust, blindmate manifold interface.

18
00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.370
This manifold sits at the back of the rack and

19
00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:24.510
serves as a shared thermal exchange interface for all DLC

20
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.170
-compatible IT gear. A key feature is the rear blindmate

21
00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:34.730
connection. Each DLC -compatible sled or chassis is fitted with

22
00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:39.010
a cold plate interface that connects seamlessly to the manifold

23
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:42.010
without requiring tools or human intervention.

24
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.070
This allows for hot swapping of gear even in liquid

25
00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:51.650
-cooled environments, reducing service downtime and risk of leaks.

26
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:56.690
The manifold itself is engineered for high flow capacity and

27
00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:02.190
thermal efficiency. It typically supports 12mm quick disconnect couplings,

28
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.730
but the spec allows flexibility in connector design provided they

29
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.730
meet OCP -compliant standards.

30
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:15.570
It's also modular, enabling single or multi -loop configurations to

31
00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.810
accommodate variable thermal loads within the same rack.

32
00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:25.530
ORv3 also accommodates coolant distribution units, or CDUs, located

33
00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:28.910
externally or internally, depending on deployment.

34
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.370
These CDUs circulate and manage coolant through the rack loop,

35
00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:37.910
often interfacing with facility -side cooling systems such as cooling

36
00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.910
towers or heat exchangers.

37
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:45.610
Another ORv3 advantage is sustainability through higher thermal set

38
00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:50.530
points. By allowing safe operation at higher inlet temperatures, often

39
00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:56.610
in the 27°C to 32°C range, ORv3

40
00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.050
racks reduce the energy needed for chilling, aligning with ASHRAE

41
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:05.170
A1 standards and enabling broader use of free cooling or

42
00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.610
warm water cooling loops.

43
00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.870
Finally, air flow and liquid cooling are not mutually exclusive.

44
00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:18.070
Many ORv3 deployments adopt hybrid cooling strategies, combining air

45
00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:23.010
-cooled IT gear with liquid -cooled accelerators or GPUs in

46
00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.850
the same rack. The rack design supports this mixed configuration

47
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:31.570
through flexible mounting and airflow containment options.

48
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:38.110
Together, these cooling innovations make ORv3 a highly adaptable platform

49
00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.330
for future -ready thermal management.

50
00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:45.690
Whether you're operating traditional servers or AI clusters pushing

51
00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.370
100 kW per rack,

